  "status_text": "Two flips can nearly halve the work across sixteen groups of switches. Lean checked this for groups of 64 switches that take turns, with earlier groups all on, later groups all off and a separate input marking each group that has started (L-lib-1333). For the active group, a light reports each pair of switches that are both on. Two NOT gates and 16,256 AND or OR gates suffice. With zero NOT gates, at least 32,256 AND or OR gates are needed. Next we can test what happens when the groups stop taking turns.",
